---
args: { request: ProcurementReviewRequest, agreementFile: AgreementDeskFile, prior?: ProcurementCheckpoint|null }
returns: ProcurementProgramResult
uses: [procurementDesk/frameNeed, procurementDesk/selectCurrentProcurementPolicy, procurementDesk/pinCatalogVersion, procurementDesk/recheckExpiredTerms, procurementDesk/aggregateCommitments, procurementDesk/verifyEntityCoverage, procurementDesk/repriceBundleRemoval, procurementDesk/interpretPurchaseNeed, procurementDesk/scopeAgreementToLegalEntity, procurementDesk/compareLineTerms, procurementDesk/constructCompliantOptions, procurementDesk/routeCumulativeApproval]
---
Bind saved = prior when supplied, otherwise null. Bind catalogPin = pinCatalogVersion(request, agreementFile.catalogVersions) and expiry = recheckExpiredTerms(request, agreementFile.waitingApprovals) before using a pending approval. Expired terms require refreshed price and scope evidence. Bind goal = frameNeed(request, agreementFile.purchases) and policy = selectCurrentProcurementPolicy(request, agreementFile.policyCandidates).

Bind intent = interpretPurchaseNeed(request, agreementFile.purchases, agreementFile.evidencePages). Recover purpose, line identity, quantity, entity and essential function from the supported purchasing record. Keep any missing decisive fact in the stage's unresolved questions. Do not select a supplier item from an unresolved intent.
Bind entity = verifyEntityCoverage(request, agreementFile.entityCoverageTerms), commitments = aggregateCommitments(request, agreementFile.relatedCommitments), and repricing = repriceBundleRemoval(request, agreementFile.bundlePriceSchedules). These guardrails are evaluated even when purchase intent is incomplete, so cumulative thresholds, affiliate scope and changed bundle terms remain visible.

Bind agreement = scopeAgreementToLegalEntity(request, intent, agreementFile.evidencePages, agreementFile.entityCoverageTerms). Match exact legal entity, agreement, schedule, intended category/use, territory, dates and amendments. If intent has no accepted purchase lines or entity scope is unresolved, preserve that blocker and produce no accepted agreement scope. Bind conformance = compareLineTerms(intent, agreement, agreementFile.bundlePriceSchedules, agreementFile.catalogVersions), keeping functional scope distinct from price compliance. Bind options = constructCompliantOptions(intent, agreement, conformance, repricing); only supported line needs and exact agreement coverage can produce an accepted option. Bind disposition = routeCumulativeApproval(request, options, commitments, agreement, expiry, policy); aggregate related commitments before routing and keep release blocked on expired or unsupported terms.

Bind checkpoint = reconcileProcurementCheckpoint(saved, request, agreementFile, intent, agreement, options, disposition). Preserve legal-entity scope, catalog edition, cumulative approval and commitment evidence separately. An expired term invalidates only pending decisions relying on it; removal from a bundle requires exact reprice evidence. A proposal is never an order release receipt. Return { caseId: request.caseId, goal, policy, intent, agreement, conformance, options, disposition, guardrails: [catalogPin, expiry, commitments, entity, repricing], checkpoint, commitAllowed: false } as ProcurementProgramResult. When essential intent is unresolved, agreement, conformance, options and disposition remain typed blocked stage results; no supplier item is selected.
